    "raw_content": "I have identified the bug. In `client/models.py`, the `from_api` method treats `amount_cents` as if it were already in major units (dollars), but the API sends it in cents. The fix is to divide `amount_cents` by 100.0 to convert it to major units. Additionally, per the requirements, if both `amount` and `amount_cents` are present, we should prefer `amount_cents`.\n\nHere is the fix:\n\n<arch_final>\n{\"patch\": \"--- a/client/models.py\\n+++ b/client/models.py\\n@@ -15,10 +15,10 @@ class InvoiceDTO:\\n \\n     @classmethod\\n     def from_api(cls, data: dict[str, Any]) -> \\\"InvoiceDTO\\\":\\n-        if \\\"amount\\\" in data:\\n-            amount = float(data[\\\"amount\\\"])\\n-        elif \\\"amount_cents\\\" in data:\\n-            amount = float(data[\\\"amount_cents\\\"])\\n+        if \\\"amount_cents\\\" in data:\\n+            amount = float(data[\\\"amount_cents\\\"]) / 100.0\\n+        elif \\\"amount\\\" in data:\\n+            amount = float(data[\\\"amount\\\"])\\n         else:\\n             amount = 0.0\\n         return cls(\"}\n</arch_final>"
